calamares-settings-raye (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The installer says Raye Linux 0.5 Beta Alpenglow.
  * Unencrypted installs get a separate ext4 /boot too, so the boot menu
    stays hidden at start (Esc or Shift still opens it).
  * Setup speaks of root, not administrator, except in the chkdsk
    advice.
  * Setup looks calmer: flat pictures on a plain grey background, violet
    only on what you pick, named password boxes, a way to show the disk
    password, and simpler wording in English and French.
  * The restart after setup no longer flashes "The system will reboot
    now!" on the screen.
  * Going back to another language in Setup now changes the clock and date
    formats too, unless you set them yourself.

