calamares-settings-raye (0.1~dev4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Wi-Fi is now a page of the installer, right after the language and
    the keyboard. Once online, the time zone is set from the location;
    offline, it is picked from two lists.
  * Wi-Fi networks joined during setup are kept in the new system.
  * Encrypted installs get a recovery key, shown at first login and never
    sent anywhere, and unlock through the TPM when the computer has one,
    bound to Secure Boot only so updates do not trigger the recovery
    prompt. Without the TPM the boot asks for the password.
  * Before starting, the disks are checked for BitLocker, a hibernated
    Windows and another system sharing EFI/ubuntu, with what to do.
  * The graphics driver is installed during setup when online.

